    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="1abce89f-05e6-5e87-8692-87213625f023" activityNameId="b834ee74-c475-564d-b3d7-6cbbf1006657" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, natural gas, allocation exergy, at PEM fuel cell 2kWe, future</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, natural gas, allocation exergy, at PEM fuel cell 2kWe, future
The multioutput-process 'natural gas, burned in PEM fuel cell 2kWe delivers the coproducts 'heat, natural gas, allocation exergy, at PEM fuel cell 2kWe' and 'electricity, natural gas, allocation exergy, at PEM fuel cell 2kWe'. The exergy allocation is the allocation scheme suggested to be used within the ecoinvent database (e.g. in electricity mixes).;
UUID: 67b9d212-8f17-36b0-bb3e-61361c26f0ad
The module includes fuel input, infrastructure and emissions to air.
Location: Natural gas input modelled for Switzerland. Process applicable in central European conditions.
Technology: polymer electrolyte membrane (PEM) fuel cell for stationary cogeneration. Performance, stack lifetime and catalyst use according to expected future values for a serial product. Operation with connection to low pressure gas network. Electrical efficiency 32%, total efficiency 87%.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data and manufacturer information 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_67b9d212-8f17-36b0-bb3e-61361c26f0ad.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
